=== TWO CONTRACT FINDINGS (fix before stage 4 / WASI factoring) ===
 1. present(at-ns) IS NOT USABLE. A guest cannot name a host monotonic instant
    sharing an origin with the host clock (host monotonic_now_ns uses its own
    Instant origin). Player passes at_ns=0 and self-paces. LEAD: on-frame hands
    the guest `nanos` — likely the shared timeline; verify and make
    monotonic_now_ns use the SAME source, or add a now()-style verb.
 2. Decode-ahead is UNBOUNDED (back-pressure hits = 0). queue-full is specified
    but nothing triggers it; a guest could decode a whole file into host memory.
 3. (stage-1 gap, CONFIRMED) the SCHEDULED queue is drained ONLY by
    composite_video_surfaces, so surfaceless/--run-once guests never present
    scheduled frames. --run-once is a deliberate special case: DO NOT change it.

=== HARDWARE PICTURE (three drivers, three different answers) ===
 fedora i965 : min none    | VA|KERNEL_DRM|DRM_PRIME | t1 OK   t2 OK   t3 OK | 300/300 PASS
 WSL d3d12   : min 64x64   | advertises DRM_PRIME_2  | t1 FAIL t2 OK   t3 OK | DECODE HANGS
 popos NVDEC : min 48x16   | reports NO mem types    | t1 FAIL t2 FAIL t3 OK | 32/300 then DPB errors
 * WSL/d3d12 decode is broken AT THE DRIVER (ffmpeg -hwaccel vaapi hangs too; sw
   decode 0.32s). Not our bug. Do not sink more time there.
 * NVDEC 32/300 + "No ShortTerm reference found": hypothesis = we allocate a FRESH
   VA surface per frame and never pool, exhausting NVDEC's decode-surface pool
   (~32 = typical NVDEC DPB). A surface pool now looks REQUIRED for NVDEC (it was
   correctly ruled out as the cause of the WSL hang).
 * Upstream cros-codecs hardcodes a 16x16 placeholder context — WRONG on 2 of 3
   drivers. Our vendored patch queries the driver. Capability bits lie in BOTH
   directions; always probe.

